# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored. No exchange keys are used anywhere.
# Only needed to call Jev yourself (python -m jevtrade.collect / jevtrade.decision);
# the hourly collect workflow reads it from the OPENROUTER_API_KEY repository secret:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional. The API reads the data-log branch from GitHub; the repo is public, so
# no token is needed, but one with read-only "Contents" access lifts GitHub's rate
# limit. With "Actions: read and write" too, JEVTRADE_KICK=1 starts the hourly
# collect run whenever GitHub's schedule skips an hour (see README, "Live website"):
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
